    {
      "id": 31,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 96
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**L0 SSTs climbing toward the stall threshold**, or **any backpressure/stall rate > 0**, means compaction is losing to the write rate \u2192 check compactor throughput and object-store latency next.\n\n**Object-store error rate > 0** \u2014 check *which* api first: sustained errors on put/get/delete point at the storage backend (S3/Tigris/network); api=\"head\" errors are often just expected 404s from existence-probing and less concerning on their own. **p99 latency spiking** on any api does point at the storage backend.\n\n**Cache hit rate dropping** under steady traffic usually means the working set has outgrown the block cache; **rising filter false-positive rate** means more unnecessary SST reads per lookup than expected.\n\n**WAL buffer backlog growing unbounded** (not just oscillating with `-flush`) means WAL flush is falling behind \u2014 check object-store PUT latency in the panel above."
      }
    },
